From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman: CC/HM VLAN-route support, dedup, and debugfs tests (T-M6-8)

Consolidates the T-M6-8 VLAN CC/HM front-end series into a single patch.
This squashes eleven originally-separate incremental patches (0121,
0121a, 0121c-0121l) that were split into per-step review slices during
ASK2 development; each slice touched the same handful of files as its
predecessor and had to apply in the exact micro-order recorded below.
Content is unchanged from the union of those patches as verified in CI
(run 34552869475, checkpoints 4c03ccf5ad29..c9f00727a3d8); only the
patch boundary is different.

Squashed originals (in real, alphabetical apply order -- the series
file's line order does NOT control apply order, find|sort does):
  0121   - dpaa-export-cc-target-resolvers
  0121a  - fman-pcd-hm-vlan-dedup
  0121c  - fman-pcd-cc-test-vlan-hm
  0121d  - fman-pcd-hm-vlan-route-dedup
  0121e  - fman-pcd-cc-test-vlan-route
  0121f  - fman-pcd-cc-test-teardown-quiesce
  0121g  - fman-pcd-cc-test-vlan-coex
  0121h  - fman-cc-miss-fe-production-api
  0121i  - fman-export-fe-root-offset (previously given a separate,
           purely cosmetic series-file slot after 0153 in the belief
           that series-file order affects apply order; it does not --
           0121i genuinely applies here, right after 0121h, in every
           real build. That belief is now moot since there is only one
           patch.)
  0121j  - fman-pcd-hm-vlan-route-translate
  0121k  - fman-pcd-cc-max-keys-64
  0121l  - fman-pcd-cc-ekfc-port-id

Touches: drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/dpaa/dpaa_eth.c,
dpaa_fman_caps.{c,h}; drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c,
fman_pcd_cc.c, fman_pcd_cc_test.c, fman_pcd_kg.c;
include/linux/fsl/fman_pcd.h.

